Explanation :

1. Client Layer
--> The Client is the application or user that sends a request to the Spring Boot application.
--> The Client's job is only to Send requests and Receive responses.
2. Controller Layer
--> The Controller is the entry point of the application.
--> It receives requests from clients and sends responses back.
--> Annotation used is @RestController
--> Responsibile for Receive & Return HTTP Request, Read parameters and Call Service Layer
3. Service Layer
--> The Service Layer contains business logic.
--> Annotation used is @Service
--> Responsibile for Business Logic only
4. Repository Layer
--> Repository Layer communicates with the database.
--> Annotation used is @Repository
--> Responsibility for Insert Data[save()], Update Data[save()], Delete Data[deleteById()] and Fetch Data[findById()]
5. Database Layer
--> The Database stores the actual data.
--> Examples : MySQL, Oracle, SQL Server etc etc 

| Layer      | Responsibility                          |
| ---------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Client     | Sends requests and receives responses   |
| Controller | Handles HTTP requests and responses     |
| Service    | Contains business logic and validations |
| Repository | Communicates with database              |
| Database   | Stores actual data                      |
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Annotation          | Purpose                                                                                             | Where Used               | Example                                      |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |
| @RestController   | Marks a class as a REST API controller. Methods return data directly as JSON/XML instead of a view. | Class Level              | `@RestController`                            |
| @RequestMapping   | Defines a base URL for all methods inside a controller. Can also specify HTTP methods.              | Class/Method Level       | `@RequestMapping("/students")`               |
| @GetMapping       | Handles HTTP GET requests (Fetch Data).                                                             | Method Level             | `@GetMapping("/{id}")`                       |
| @PostMapping      | Handles HTTP POST requests (Create Data).                                                           | Method Level             | `@PostMapping("/save")`                      |
| @PutMapping       | Handles HTTP PUT requests (Update Data).                                                            | Method Level             | `@PutMapping("/{id}")`                       |
| @DeleteMapping    | Handles HTTP DELETE requests (Delete Data).                                                         | Method Level             | `@DeleteMapping("/{id}")`                    |
| @PathVariable     | Reads a value from the URL path and assigns it to a method parameter.                               | Method Parameter         | `@PathVariable Long id`                      |
| @RequestBody      | Converts JSON data from the request body into a Java object.                                        | Method Parameter         | `@RequestBody Student student`               |
| @Autowired        | Automatically injects a bean (Dependency Injection).                                                | Field/Constructor/Setter | `@Autowired private StudentService service;` |
| @Service          | Marks a class as a Service Layer bean containing business logic.                                    | Class Level              | `@Service`                                   |
| @Repository       | Marks a class/interface as a Repository Layer bean for database operations.                         | Class Level              | `@Repository`                                |
